## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates your ability to enable rapid domain adaptation with privacy guarantees in a real-time environment, emphasizing latency constraints, privacy preservation, and robust rollback mechanisms.

## Key Concepts

- Parameter-efficient adapters (LoRA/Adapters) for domain adaptation
- On-device fine-tuning with privacy guarantees (DP or federated learning)
- Streaming drift detection and safe rollback strategies

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo: load base model, attach adapter for domain, fine-tune on small labeled set
function adaptDomain(model, domain, labeledData) {
  const adapter = new LoRAAdapter(model, { rank: 4, alpha: 8 });
  adapter.fineTune(labeledData, { privacy: 'DP-SGD', epochs: 3 });
  return adapter;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Probes on-device NLP, privacy, and latency trade-offs in edge deployments typical of Cloudflare/Uber-scale products.

## Key Concepts

- On-device inference with deterministic latency
- Regex-based redaction plus tiny ML for edge cases
- Multilingual and code-switching handling
- Privacy controls and local data labeling

## Code Example

```javascript
const redact = (text) => {
  const emails = /[\w.+-]+@[\w.-]+\.[a-zA-Z]{2,}/g;
  const phones = /(\+?\d[\d\s\-\(\)]{7,}\d)/g;
  let out = text.replace(emails, "[REDACTED_EMAIL]");
  out = out.replace(phones, "[REDACTED_PHONE]");
  out = out.replace(/\b[A-Z][a-z]+ [A-Z][a-z]+\b/g, "[REDACTED_NAME]");
  return out;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you measure and guarantee 100 ms latency across devices?
- How would you handle false positives and user-triggered corrections without server contact?

